#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Writes the lightning slime's seven animation prompts (2026-11-09) into Animations/LightningSlime/<folder>/source/<folder>_gemini_prompt.txt.
The ice slime's prompts (Animations/IceSlime/<folder>/source) are the templates: same panel counts, poses, percentages and timing, so the page's code for each skill can be reused; only the material
(electric-yellow jelly, solid bolt-shaped spikes, crisp blue-white arcs, tiny zigzag bolts) and the lessons of the lightning idle sheet are new.
  python Animations/LightningSlime/source/write_prompts.py
"""
import os

ROOT = os.path.abspath(os.path.join(os.path.dirname(__file__), "..", "..", ".."))

CHARACTER = """CHARACTER: the exact same character as in the attached reference image: the LIGHTNING SLIME, in exactly the painted look of the reference. A low dome of matte electric-yellow jelly with golden-amber shading, wider than tall, with a flat skirt-like base that spreads on the floor in a smooth, slightly wavy rim. A thin dark umber-brown outline around the body (not black, not white). The round pockets (craters) and the hairline cyan-white crackle veins on the body exactly as in the reference. The face: heavy slanted angry brows with a wrinkled forehead, two narrow slanted eyes with glowing pale cyan-white pupils, and the jagged mouth with the thin cyan-white electric line along it, exactly as in the reference. No arms, no legs, no ears, no horns, no teeth. A crown of tall jagged bolt-shaped yellow spikes rises from the top and back of its head and a spike grows out of each side of the body (the left one longer), exactly as in the reference: solid yellow with cream tips and darker amber facets, thin dark outline, fully opaque. A few tiny solid zigzag bolts (yellow-white and some cyan-white) float around and above the crown. Round the body and the spikes crackle thin jagged lightning arcs in cyan-white with an azure edge and a thin navy outline, drawn crisp and opaque, exactly in the style of the reference. Keep the same painted style, colours, spikes and face. Do not redesign anything."""

VIEW = """VIEW: the same three-quarter view as in the reference, the whole body and the face turned about 30 degrees towards the RIGHT edge of the panel, as if looking at an enemy standing on the right. The view does not change in any panel: the face never turns, and it stays in the same place on the body."""

SOFT = """NO SOFT EFFECTS: no glow, no light halo, no bloom, no blur, no haze, no see-through anything, no gradient fade-outs, no sparkle flares or light rays, no light spilling onto the background. The arcs are crisp too: thin hard-edged opaque zigzags with a navy outline, nothing soft round them. Every spike, bolt and arc has a hard, clean, opaque edge. No scorch marks, no puddle, no cast shadow, no motion lines, no impact stars, no text."""

LESSONS = """LESSONS FROM THE EARLIER SHEETS (docs/MONSTERS.md): the generator exaggerates stretches and leaps (asked 16% for a leap's top, drew 31%) but UNDER-delivers a shrink (asked 28%, drew 38%); it draws the bottom row of a sheet bigger than the top row (the cut corrects what is left); it ignored 'no shadow' once (a shadow ellipse under a floating body) and 'on the floor line' once (poses drawn in the air), which the cutter copes with; it fills its panels. The LIGHTNING IDLE sheet taught two more things: the arcs vanished completely in two of its six panels and the mouth's cyan line went brown in one, so every prompt below says that the arcs and the mouth line are in EVERY panel; and some arcs ran over the skirt and hung below it, so the prompts say to keep them off the skirt and the floor. The slime's spikes are SOLID like the ice slime's crystals: the crown never bends or flickers (the fire slime's flames did); only the arcs and the tiny floating bolts move freely."""

ARCS_ALWAYS = "THE ARCS: in EVERY panel four to eight thin crisp arcs (cyan-white with an azure edge and a navy outline) run along the body and the spikes and leap a short way into the air, a DIFFERENT set in each panel, never none. They never cross the face (eyes, brows, mouth) and never touch the skirt or the floor: they stay on the upper two thirds of the body and in the air above and beside it. {extra}"

BACKGROUND = """BACKGROUND AND LAYOUT: one flat pure magenta (#FF00FF) background filling the whole image, identical in every pixel. No gradient, floor, ground line, shadow, glow or vignette. NO GRID LINES, NO BORDERS and no black lines between or around the panels. No text, numbers or labels. No magenta, pink or violet tint on the creature or the arcs; its outline is dark umber-brown (the arcs' navy) and hard-edged."""

REPLIES = """- Replies if it goes wrong. {specific}If it draws glow, haze or a halo: "Redo it. NO glow, NO haze, NO halo: every arc is a thin, hard-edged, opaque zigzag with a thin navy outline, on the flat magenta background." If arcs are missing in some panels or the mouth line goes dark: "Redo it. EVERY panel has the thin blue arcs round the body and spikes (a different set in each panel, four to eight of them) and the cyan-white electric line along the mouth." If arcs cover the face or touch the skirt: "Redo it. No arc crosses the eyes, brows or mouth and none touches the skirt or the floor: the arcs stay on the upper two thirds of the body and in the air." If it turns orange, green or blue-bodied: "Redo it. Keep the matte electric yellow body, the brown outline and the cyan-white blue arcs of the attached picture." If the spikes change shape or bend: "Redo it. The spikes are solid: the crown is exactly the same spikes in the same places in every panel and only moves with the body." If it turns glossy, pale or black-outlined: "Redo it. Keep the matte mid-saturated yellow painted look and the thin dark umber outline of the attached picture." If it grows teeth, a tongue, arms or legs: "Redo it. No teeth, no tongue, no arms, no legs." If the panels overlap, are unequal or cut: "Redo it. Equal panels, no grid lines, each creature fully inside its own panel with empty margin round it." """

ANIMS = []

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- 1. SPARK SPIT (attack)
ANIMS.append(dict(
    folder="spark_spit", title="SPARK SPIT (the basic attack, 8 frames, 4 x 2)", ice="frost_spit", ice_sheet="frost_spit_sheet.jpg", tag="spit", cols=4, rows=2, ratio="2:1 (or 16:9)",
    intro="The lightning twin of the ice slime's Frost Spit and the fire slime's Ember Spit (the same 8 poses and timing, so the page reuses the release frame 5 and the holds); the name and what it does are placeholders (docs/MONSTERS.md).",
    what="""WHAT IT IS. The slime rears back, puffs up, opens its mouth with a bright cyan-white spark inside it and spits it at the enemy, then springs back. It is a ranged attack: the slime does NOT travel to the enemy; it stays on its floor spot and only leans and stretches forward. THE SPIT ITSELF IS NOT DRAWN IN THE SHEET: the flying ball of electricity, its trail and its impact are added by the page, starting at the mouth on the release frame (frame 5). So no panel may show a projectile, a bolt, a lightning beam or an arc flying out of the mouth; the open mouth only shows a bright spark ball sitting inside it.""",
    check="(1) the same lightning slime in all eight panels (face, spikes, yellow matte look, outline, arcs); (2) panels 1 and 8 are the idle's rest pose; (3) the base always touches the same floor line, its back (left) end stays on the same spot, the body only leans and stretches toward the right; (4) the mouth: closed jagged mouth with its cyan line in 1 to 3, a small opening with a bright cyan-white spark ball inside in 4, wide open in 5 and 6, closing in 7; (5) NOTHING leaves the mouth; (6) the spike crown is the same solid crown in every panel and only leans with the body; (7) arcs in every panel, a different set each time, never over the face or the skirt; (8) every part crisp and opaque, no glow; (9) the same size in all panels (the bottom row not bigger), nothing touches a panel edge or overlaps its neighbour; (10) no GIF and no extra images.",
    cut="the ice spit's cut (`Animations/IceSlime/frost_spit/source/make_*_strip.py`) with the lightning panel loader (`Animations/LightningSlime/source/light_panels.py`: body measured from its warm colours) into `Animations/LightningSlime/spark_spit/lightning_spark_spit_8frame_strip.png` (slot `attack`), about 12 fps, release frame 5, with the mouth's place on frames 4 to 6 measured from the bright spark (`.mouth.json`). The page then needs the lightning spit: a crackling spark ball flung from the mouth (the mage's lightning / the Rogue's electricity), placeholder effect.",
    specific='If a projectile or lightning leaves the mouth: "Redo it. Nothing leaves the mouth in any panel: no bolt, no arc, no beam, no flying spark. The mouth only shows a bright spark ball inside it. The spit is added later." If it is too wild: "Redo it. The slime does not jump and does not leave the floor: its base always touches the same floor line. It only leans back a little (up to 8 degrees) and then forward a little (up to 8 degrees); the body is at most 12% lower in the coil and 8% longer in the spit." ',
    body="""THE MOUTH: in the reference the mouth is a jagged grimace with a thin cyan-white electric line along it. For the spit it opens: in the panels where it is open it is a plain, round or oval opening with a thin dark outline, its inside a deep dark umber-brown with a bright cyan-white SPARK (a small crisp solid round ball with a thin navy outline, fully INSIDE the mouth) at the back of it. No teeth, no tongue. The spark never leaves the mouth. In the panels where the mouth is closed it is the jagged mouth with its cyan line as in the reference.

NOTHING FLIES OUT: no projectile, no bolt in flight, no lightning beam, no arc leaving the mouth, no stream of sparks, no breath in any panel. The spit is added later by the game. The only electricity in the panels is the slime's own thin arcs round the body, its spikes, and its tiny floating bolts.

{soft} No impact stars.

SAME SCALE AND FLOOR (very important): draw the creature at the same size in all eight panels: the second row must NOT be drawn bigger than the first row. In panel 1 the BASE of the slime, its flat underside (not counting any arc), is about 50% of the panel width, and its lowest point is about 86% down the panel. The base touches the same floor line in every panel and never leaves it: no hop, no jump. The BACK (left) end of the base stays on the same spot in every panel; the body leans and stretches forward (to the right) only in panels 5 and 6, where the front of the base may reach at most about 8% of the base width further to the right. Do not zoom in or out between panels. The slime is wide: its whole body, spikes and arcs must fit inside the MIDDLE 80% of its panel's width, with clear empty margin on the left and right, and at least 10% empty margin above and below. If the panels are tall, leave empty space above and below instead of drawing the creature bigger.

HOW MUCH MOVES (moderate: bigger than a breath, but a small slime, not a bounce):
THE BODY: in the coil (panels 3 and 4) the dome is about 12% lower than in panel 1 and a little wider, and the whole body leans BACK (away from the enemy, to the left) by about 8 degrees; in the spit (panels 5 and 6) it springs forward: the dome leans forward (to the right) by about 8 degrees, is about 6% taller than at rest and about 8% longer toward the right. No other deformation: it stays a dome with a skirt, never a tall column or a flat pancake.
THE SPIKE CROWN: solid, it never bends, grows, shrinks or flickers: in every panel it is the same crown of spikes, in the same places, with the same shapes, and it only moves WITH the body (it leans and rides up and down with the dome as one rigid piece).
THE SKIRT: the rim of the base ripples a little in the coil and the spit; the base as a whole keeps its floor line.
{arcs}
THE FLOATING BOLTS: the tiny zigzag bolts are blown back (left) a little by the spit in panels 5 and 6 and drift back in 7 and 8.

THE EIGHT FRAMES:
1. Rest. Exactly the pose of the reference image and of the idle's rest pose: the same body, face, crown, arcs and bolts, the mouth the closed jagged mouth with its cyan line.
2. Gather. The dome sinks about 5% and the body starts to lean back about 4 degrees. The brows lower, the eyes narrow. The mouth is still closed.
3. Coil. The deepest crouch: the dome about 12% lower than in panel 1, a little wider, leaning back about 8 degrees, the face tilted a little upward. The sides of the face puff out a little as if the cheeks were full. The mouth pressed shut, the brows low and fierce. The arcs gathered close to the body.
4. Charge. Still coiled, the body trembles: the rim ripples more. The mouth opens a little into a small dark opening and a small bright cyan-white spark ball shows inside it (fully inside the mouth).
5. Spit. The RELEASE frame. The body springs forward: the dome leans forward about 8 degrees, about 6% taller than at rest, the face thrust forward to the right, the mouth wide open, round, with a bright spark ball at the back of it. The crown leans with the body, the arcs and bolts blown back. Nothing has left the mouth yet or ever.
6. Follow-through. The farthest forward point: the body stretched about 8% longer to the right, the mouth wide open and now empty, still bright inside, beginning to close.
7. Recoil. The body snaps back: the dome about 4% lower than at rest, leaning back about 3 degrees, the mouth closing to a small opening, the rim rippling.
8. Settle. Almost the rest pose of panel 1: the mouth closed with its cyan line, the arcs and bolts nearly as in panel 1 but not an exact copy. This is the pose just before the idle starts again.""",
    arcs_extra="In the coil (3, 4) they gather closer to the body (shorter); in the spit (5, 6) they are blown back (left) a little.",
    final="Eight equal panels, 4 columns by 2 rows. The slime stays on the floor in one place and only leans and stretches; nothing leaves its mouth; the mouth shows a bright spark ball inside in panels 4 to 6; the spike crown is solid and only moves with the body; thin crisp blue arcs in every panel (a different set each time, never over the face or the skirt); NO glow, no haze, no orange or red; the same size in all panels and each fully inside its own panel.",
))

